\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The first Nowell the angel did say
\par Was to certain poor shepherds in fields as they lay:
\par In fields where they lay a-keeping their sheep
\par On a cold winter's night that was so deep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Nowell, Nowell, 
\par Nowell, Nowell,
\par Born is the King of Israel.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. They looked up and saw a star,
\par Shining in the east, beyond them far,
\par And to the earth it gave great light,
\par And so it continued both day and night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Nowell, Nowell, 
\par Nowell, Nowell,
\par Born is the King of Israel.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And by the light of that same star,
\par Three wise men came from country far;
\par To seek for a King was their intent,
\par And to follow the star wherever it went.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Nowell, Nowell, 
\par Nowell, Nowell,
\par Born is the King of Israel.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. This star drew nigh to the north-west,
\par O'er Bethlehem it took its rest,
\par And there it did both stop and stay
\par Right over the place where Jesus lay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Nowell, Nowell, 
\par Nowell, Nowell,
\par Born is the King of Israel.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then let us all with one accord,
\par Sing praises to our Heavenly Lord,
\par That hath made heaven 
\par and earth of nought,
\par And with His blood mankind hath bought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Nowell, Nowell, 
\par Nowell, Nowell,
\par Born is the King of Israel.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

